==English==
{{wp|Date}}
[[File:A closeup of Dates.JPG|right|thumb|Dates (fruit)]]
[[File:Date Palmtree.jpg|right|thumb|A date palm]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/deɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-date.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪt|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|fruit}}
From {{inh|en|enm|date}}, from {{der|en|fro|date}}, {{m|fro|datil}}, {{m|fro|datille}}, from {{der|en|la|dactylus}}, from {{der|en|grc|δάκτυλος|t=finger}} (from the resemblance of the date to a human finger), probably a folk-etymological alteration of a word from a Semitic source such as {{der|en|ar|دَقَل|t=variety of date palm}} or {{der|en|he|דֶּקֶל|tr=deqel|t=date palm}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The [[fruit]] of the [[date palm]], {{taxfmt|Phoenix dactylifera|species}}, somewhat in the shape of an [[olive]], containing a soft, sweet pulp and enclosing a hard kernel.
#: {{ux|en|We made a nice cake from '''dates'''.}}
# The [[date palm]].
#: {{ux|en|There were a few '''dates''' planted around the house.}}

