====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To note the time or place of writing or executing; to express in an instrument the time of its execution.
#: {{ux|en|to '''date''' a letter, a bond, a deed, or a charter}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1699|author=w:Joseph Addison|title=Letter to Rt. Hon. Charles Montagu, Esq.|location=Blois, France|newversion=republished in|title2=The Life of Joseph Addison|2ndauthor=w:Lucy Aikin|chapter2=3|volume2=1|location2=Longman, Brown, Green, and Longmans|year2=1843|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=w0oJAAAAQAAJ&lpg=PA79&ots=9zDqzFtT9E&pg=PA79|page2=79|passage=You will be surprised, I don't question, to find among your correspondencies in foreign parts, a letter '''dated''' from Blois.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year2=1801|date=1796-01-01|author=w:William Cobbett|title=A New Year's Gift to the Democrats|title2=Porcupine's Works|others=footnote|newversion=republished in|location2=London|publisher2=For Cobbett and Morgan|volume2=2|pageurl2=http://books.google.com/books?id=KNRKAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA430&dq=%22The+letter+is+dated+at+Philadelphia%22&hl=en&ei=BFyNTrWhIueNmQW7xvkd&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CDMQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=%22The%20letter%20is%20dated%20at%20Philadelphia%22&f=false|page2=430|passage=I keep to the very words of the letter; but that, by "this State," is meant the State of Pennsylvania, cannot be doubted, especially when we see that the letter is '''dated''' at Philadelphia.}}
#* {{RQ:Arnold Essays in Criticism|page=281|passage=In these countries much of his Journal seems to have been written; parts of it are '''dated''' from them; and there, a few weeks before his fifty-ninth birthday, he fell sick and died.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To note or fix the time of (an event); to give the date of.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James George Frazer|title=The Golden Bough|year=1911|volume=10|page=202|text=The writer '''dates''' the festival on June 21st, which is probably a mistake.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To determine the age of something.
#: {{ux|en|to '''date''' the building of the pyramids}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To take (someone) on a [[#Noun|date]], or a series of dates.
# {{lb|en|transitive|by extension}} To have a steady relationship with; to be romantically involved with.
#: {{syn|en|go out|see|Thesaurus:date}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2008-05-15|work=NEWS.com.au|title=Jessica Simpson upset John Mayer dating Jennifer Aniston|passage=Jessica Simpson reportedly went on a drinking binge after discovering ex-boyfriend John Mayer is '''dating''' Jennifer Aniston.}}
# {{lb|en|reciprocal|by extension}} To have a steady relationship with each other; to be romantically involved with each other.
#: {{syn|en|go out|see|Thesaurus:date}}
#: {{ux|en|They met a couple of years ago, but have been '''dating''' for about five months.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To make or become old, especially in such a way as to fall out of fashion, become less appealing or attractive, etc.
#: {{syn|en|age|elden|obsolesce|Thesaurus:to age}}
#: {{ux|en|This show hasn't '''dated''' well.}}
#: {{ux|en|The comedian '''dated''' himself by making quips about bands from the 1960s.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1971-04-30|title=Research by Experiment|journal={{w|Nature (journal)|Nature}}|volume=230|issue=5296|doi=10.1038/230602b0|page=603|passage=In these days of decimalization and metrication it is a pity that SI units were not used as this will '''date''' a very useful little book prematurely.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|with ''from''}} To have beginning; to begin; to be dated or reckoned.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1826|author=w:Edward Everett|title=The Claims of Citizens of the United States of America on the Governments of Naples, Holland, and France
|passage=The Batavian republic '''dates''' from the successes of the French arms.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=Foreword|passage=He stood transfixed before the unaccustomed view of London at night time, a vast panorama which reminded him {{...}} of some wood engravings far off and magical, in a printshop in his childhood. They '''dated''' from the previous century and were coarsely printed on tinted paper, with tinsel outlining the design.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=52| magazine=w:The Economist| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/international/21579039-chinas-growing-empire-ports-abroad-mainly-about-trade-not-aggression-new-masters The new masters and commanders]| passage=From the ground, Colombo’s port does not look like much. Those entering it are greeted by wire fences, walls '''dating''' back to colonial times and security posts. For mariners leaving the port after lonely nights on the high seas, the delights of the B52 Night Club and Stallion Pub lie a stumble away.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* To note the time of writing one may say '''dated at''' or '''from''' a place.

